From: librenms-theme-selector <https://github.com/XBLOssia/librenms-theme-selector>
Subject: [PATCH] generic_data: read port series colours from config

port_bits renders through this helper, which hard-codes its six series
colours and reads no config at all. Every other shared graph helper that
carries a palette reads graph_colours.*; this one predates that mechanism
and never got converted.

Introduces graph_colours.port_in and graph_colours.port_out, each a
three-tone ramp (palest first: max fill, area fill, outline). Both default
to the values previously hard-coded here, so an instance that sets neither
key renders byte-identically - verified by comparing PNG output.

The file's other twelve literals - percentile rules, port-speed lines and
prediction overlays - are deliberately untouched. They are arguably meant
to be fixed, and leaving them out keeps the diff to one concern.

Also declares both keys in config_definitions.json. lnms config:set validates
every key against that file and refuses anything undeclared, and the only
wildcard defined is alert.macros.rule.*, so the keys have to be named.

NOTE: this is a LOCAL, TEMPORARY patch to two core files. daily.sh reverts
both on update. See scripts/patch-core.sh and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
---
--- a/includes/html/graphs/generic_data.inc.php
+++ b/includes/html/graphs/generic_data.inc.php
@@ -145,19 +145,33 @@
 }
 
 $rrd_options[] = 'COMMENT:bps      Now       Ave      Max      ' . LibrenmsConfig::get('percentile_value') . 'th %\\n';
 
-$rrd_options[] = 'AREA:in' . $format . '_max#D7FFC7' . $stacked['transparency'] . ':';
-$rrd_options[] = 'AREA:in' . $format . '#90B040' . $stacked['transparency'] . ':';
-$rrd_options[] = 'LINE:in' . $format . '#608720:In ';
+// Port traffic series colours.
+//
+// Defaults are the values this file previously hard-coded, so an instance
+// that sets neither key renders byte-identically. Each ramp is three tones,
+// palest first: the 95th-percentile max fill, the main area fill, and the
+// outline. Matches the shape of the existing graph_colours.* palettes.
+$port_series = function (string $key, array $fallback): array {
+    $v = LibrenmsConfig::get($key);
+
+    return (is_array($v) && count($v) >= 3) ? array_values($v) : $fallback;
+};
+$port_in = $port_series('graph_colours.port_in', ['D7FFC7', '90B040', '608720']);
+$port_out = $port_series('graph_colours.port_out', ['E0E0FF', '8080C0', '606090']);
+
+$rrd_options[] = 'AREA:in' . $format . '_max#' . $port_in[0] . $stacked['transparency'] . ':';
+$rrd_options[] = 'AREA:in' . $format . '#' . $port_in[1] . $stacked['transparency'] . ':';
+$rrd_options[] = 'LINE:in' . $format . '#' . $port_in[2] . ':In ';
 $rrd_options[] = 'GPRINT:in' . $format . ':LAST:%6.' . $float_precision . 'lf%s';
 $rrd_options[] = 'GPRINT:in' . $format . ':AVERAGE:%6.' . $float_precision . 'lf%s';
 $rrd_options[] = 'GPRINT:in' . $format . '_max:MAX:%6.' . $float_precision . 'lf%s';
 $rrd_options[] = 'GPRINT:percentile_in:%6.' . $float_precision . 'lf%s\\n';
 
-$rrd_options[] = 'AREA:dout' . $format . '_max#E0E0FF' . $stacked['transparency'] . ':';
-$rrd_options[] = 'AREA:dout' . $format . '#8080C0' . $stacked['transparency'] . ':';
-$rrd_options[] = 'LINE:dout' . $format . '#606090:Out';
+$rrd_options[] = 'AREA:dout' . $format . '_max#' . $port_out[0] . $stacked['transparency'] . ':';
+$rrd_options[] = 'AREA:dout' . $format . '#' . $port_out[1] . $stacked['transparency'] . ':';
+$rrd_options[] = 'LINE:dout' . $format . '#' . $port_out[2] . ':Out';
 $rrd_options[] = 'GPRINT:out' . $format . ':LAST:%6.' . $float_precision . 'lf%s';
 $rrd_options[] = 'GPRINT:out' . $format . ':AVERAGE:%6.' . $float_precision . 'lf%s';
 $rrd_options[] = 'GPRINT:out' . $format . '_max:MAX:%6.' . $float_precision . 'lf%s';
 $rrd_options[] = 'GPRINT:percentile_out:%6.' . $float_precision . 'lf%s\\n';
